} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a27c0df3-4d1c-54e1-9219-aeb6df7ad819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531217} :answer-field/id #uuid "d909fbcb-d827-5b40-9359-4b2948795876" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531531} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b820369c-81ff-58ee-a127-e2d6233a0b94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b820369c-81ff-58ee-a127-e2d6233a0b94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531258} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3e88de5-3537-5d05-b414-2095d1fba253" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531552}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5b9f6727-3d7f-553c-90bd-4d6b87d491ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-269762" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{4}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}6{y}_{1}+1 \\\\ {y}_{1}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAccording to the chain rule, the derivative \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))\n$$\n\nis the product of a$\\,\\,${{field-1}}$\\times ${{field-2}} \nmatrix with a \n{{field-3}} $\\times $ {{field-4}} \nmatrix, which results in a \n{{field-5}} $\\times $ {{field-6}} \nmatrix." :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{4}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, the product\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nof a $2\\times 2$ matrix with a $2\\times 4$ matrix is a $2\\times 4$ matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204098 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "581d60ae-7926-5d60-a348-3c7fe045db06" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Dimensions of a Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2a15cab-22a4-5667-9025-a13fecb07f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2a15cab-22a4-5667-9025-a13fecb07f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531299} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab3edcde-2370-5fc8-98a3-6c82a3052d1b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203448} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fa2bc32-5eea-5d94-9810-072ac4a32c58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fa2bc32-5eea-5d94-9810-072ac4a32c58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530891} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb489b23-1aaf-5d38-ad03-cd82617b7c10" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/t