"cb36d833-b394-57b0-9ea8-b980654e0a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb36d833-b394-57b0-9ea8-b980654e0a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531289} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fd1bbce-0ea2-5396-9310-1a1c60a15a00" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e6329401-f82b-530a-a12e-fc5e470a5471" :question/math-academy-id "q-269768" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAccording to the chain rule, the derivative \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))\n$$\n\nis the product of a$\\,\\,${{field-1}}$\\times ${{field-2}} \nmatrix with a \n{{field-3}} $\\times $ {{field-4}} \nmatrix, which results in a \n{{field-5}} $\\times $ {{field-6}} \nmatrix." :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{3}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, the product\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nof a $3\\times 2$ matrix with a $2\\times 2$ matrix is a $3\\times 2$ matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531598 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204099 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e07aa16a-05a4-5cf7-8eba-bfe287efdf88" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Composition of Vector-Valued Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d386f327-1b96-53b3-a7e0-f538b69b4b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d386f327-1b96-53b3-a7e0-f538b69b4b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531302} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bc9ae22-cb20-510a-b7a2-e6f0d1758238" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531446} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23ed8eaa-ca9f-556c-8ad7-26b7d0de8dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23ed8eaa-ca9f-556c-8ad7-26b7d0de8dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530945} :answer-field/id #uuid "942c7780-6535-5d0f-a664-a1bcb891c110" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531484} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87c362c1-bab8-5afa-ac27-6274d18e5dc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87c362c1-bab8-5afa-ac27-6274d18e5dc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531159} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2ce961c-2b93-552d-bece-02a4eefb9af4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531550}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5bd6ce37-dfc0-53de-b48f-f0c1cbf86c1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-269782" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1}+4{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{2}+8{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}(2{y}_{1}+4{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}(2{y}_{1}+4{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{2}+8{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{2}+8{y}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 2{y}_{1} & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2}+{0}^{2} \\\\ {1}^{2}-{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} & 2{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & -2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 & 0 \\\\ 20 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531577 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204099 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e07aa16a-05a4-5cf7-8eba-bfe287efdf88" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Composition of Vector-Valued Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e25c5dab-2ab7-5cc2-9a6f-58bc04896ed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e25c5dab-2ab7-5cc2-9a6f-58bc04896ed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531327} :answer-field/id #uuid "14e2587d-142c-5f42-b805-a2dc168df701" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531400} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "448a1728-0e5d-5da5-ad5c-f154b8ecf969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "448a1728-0e5d-5da5-ad5c-f154b8ecf969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531011} :answer-field/id #uuid "288a36d8-5d2d-567a-9ad2-820a7533c15d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531414} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "208e7973-c024-51f5-9e8c-860ada293675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "208e7973-c024-51f5-9e8c-860ada293675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530932} :answer-field/id #uuid "b37e9bb4-7b51-5e9d-bf67-d5f13bdb4255" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531506}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "316244d1-8305-5968-b730-d6310a788240" :question/math-academy-id "q-269795" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{3}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{2}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}+{y}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2} & {y}_{1} \\\\ 0 & 2{y}_{2} \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}-1\\cdot 1 \\\\ -1-1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & {x}_{1} \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204590 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204100 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc95d2b5-9318-58b0-aa61-963954bf4594" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Functions Defined Using Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be4fe82c-92fb-5f8f-90d3-234e29b3c139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be4fe82c-92fb-5f8f-90d3-234e29b3c139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531268} :answer-field/id #uuid "832d18af-bd7f-518b-85bf-e0448f95f2f8" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203457} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "463df682-92d8-56d8-92fc-869f6526ae63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "463df682-92d8-56d8-92fc-869f6526ae63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531015} :answer-field/id #uuid "ace94e8b-2784-55ec-8dec-d8ca07414196" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203458} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aaa93cb-9bae-57f3-aafb-1f6b7516aa22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1aaa93cb-9bae-57f3-aafb-1f6b7516aa22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530915} :answer-field/id #uuid "30484f87-275f-5ebc-970f-1cdd925b5efd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203459} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecb98ecb-5d5e-5050-a3f9-48d2a87aeb75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ecb98ecb-5d5e-5050-a3f9-48d2a87aeb75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531343} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d798401-db75-5732-82d5-1f23e01b5d3a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c19ca30a-f0fa-5057-a407-4fa3247cf47b" :question/math-academy-id "q-269799" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y(x)=Ax$ and $f(y)=By,$ where $x\\in {R}^{3},y\\in {R}^{2},$ and the matrices $A$ and $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[0,\\,-1,\\,1]^{T}?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $B$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}=B.\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =BA \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -7 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 9 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531600 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204100 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc95d2b5-9318-58b0-aa61-963954bf4594" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Functions Defined Using Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49ec15b7-9a76-5f20-9b36-a1b00add3537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49ec15b7-9a76-5f20-9b36-a1b00add3537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531022} :answer-field/id #uuid "100411ea-c301-524c-9670-31f318b91b8d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531396} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c503c8b6-cb84-522c-82af-ac0b3cdc6384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c503c8b6-cb84-522c-82af-ac0b3cdc6384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531276} :answer-field/id #uuid "b25dc009-09b5-5ac7-9218-9efff302f392" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531505} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "accc3c42-57e9-5709-b528-8e32daddf2e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "accc3c42-57e9-5709-b528-8e32daddf2e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531237} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6666e26-39f4-552b-a7aa-0c5ac20b05b6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531517} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fd01b8f-7da4-5c18-973d-007aabdade1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fd01b8f-7da4-5c18-973d-007aabdade1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530928} :answer-field/id #uuid "d50b99a6-09a2-5bf8-a1ca-65bc1edb698c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "622e64f1-e6e7-5b08-85d4-13a13c5f884f" :question/math-academy-id "q-269804" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y(x)=Ax$ and $f(y)=By,$ where $x\\in {R}^{2},y\\in {R}^{2},$ and the matrices $A$ and $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[0,\\,0]^{T}?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$16$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $B$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{3}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}=B.\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =BA \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 13 \\\\ 6 & -15 \\\\ 16 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531563 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204100 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc95d2b5-9318-58b0-aa61-963954bf4594" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Functions Defined Using Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3eb6efb2-996e-5718-b658-df34c48f6590" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3eb6efb2-996e-5718-b658-df34c48f6590" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530996} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ac0a5ce-5861-5053-9728-8c4fd1cb5e8f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531391} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec845946-3714-52e3-84bc-89dc914bbef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec845946-3714-52e3-84bc-89dc914bbef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531342} :answer-field/id #uuid "46bae893-4ebe-51de-9570-54b7da87315d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531444} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da82b557-c258-5e35-96bb-e77807d62b45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da82b557-c258-5e35-96bb-e77807d62b45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531311} :answer-field/id #uuid "62a00025-1e2a-56c1-80cf-393becfa5240" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "19d96d91-ae11-5a12-a4f6-96b41a2e839b" :question/math-academy-id "q-269811" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y(x)=Ax$ and $f(y)=By,$ where $x\\in {R}^{2},y\\in {R}^{3},$ and the matrices $A$ and $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[3,\\,1]^{T}?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{3}$ by multiplying it by $B$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}=B.\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{3}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =BA \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -9 \\\\ 13 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531627 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204100 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc95d2b5-9318-58b0-aa61-963954bf4594" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Functions Defined Using Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cf884bc-7208-554a-9246-1064a959796f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cf884bc-7208-554a-9246-1064a959796f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531068} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bf943b9-df94-524e-bcf5-9dc4bf043905" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531420} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bff7b7c-75ce-5613-b082-0122e4795875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bff7b7c-75ce-5613-b082-0122e4795875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531199} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d1e6843-8b9f-57b5-9c3f-415b575af25c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531465} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e950d749-747e-5c10-9923-7ecc4c4e753b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e950d749-747e-5c10-9923-7ecc4c4e753b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531333} :answer-field/id #uuid "763c8765-a9b1-5269-af33-608777d3259f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a62becc2-1daf-5292-96cb-be1f422032a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-269812" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y(x)=Ax$ and $f(y)=By,$ where $x\\in {R}^{2},y\\in {R}^{3},$ and the matrices $A$ and $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[3,\\,-2]^{T}?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{3}$ by multiplying it by $B$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}=B.\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{3}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =BA \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 23 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531614 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204101 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "12de0411-fa8a-5be0-9d80-3e174cf92707" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Composition of Three Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a94cb7e-93fa-5ae6-867e-dd055216d295" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & 20 \\\\ 20 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530914} {:answer/id #uuid "4e5f0dcf-acb7-567f-b3d0-d286714d4078" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 30 \\\\ 20 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531032} {:answer/id #uuid "b72d5e70-4fb9-584a-8ad9-758dba2d99ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}20 & 3 \\\\ 20 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531256} {:answer/id #uuid "bc5cce69-f255-593b-8730-23f6d96f322f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}20 & 30 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531263} {:answer/id #uuid "df39de81-d0d3-5654-a882-36abf60eaa20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}20 & 30 \\\\ 20 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df39de81-d0d3-5654-a882-36abf60eaa20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}20 & 30 \\\\ 20 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531320} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd196ff8-da06-5ece-8bd7-2692100d1ca4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84a8217d-9b8f-5f74-ba0c-1dc1b7379e21" :question/math-academy-id "q-269816" :question/problem "For $x,y,z\\in {R}^{2},$ consider the following functions: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & y(x)=Ax\\,\\text{where}\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & z(y)=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}-{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & f(z)=Cz\\,\\text{where}\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(z(y(x)))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(z(y(x)))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $z\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $C$ and outputs a vector $f(z)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}=C.\n$$\n\n- The function $z$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $z(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{z}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{z}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{z}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{z}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=A{x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(z(y(x))){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}{|}_{{z}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}20 & 30 \\\\ 20 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531637 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204101 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "12de0411-fa8a-5be0-9d80-3e174cf92707" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Composition of Three Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "086b120f-84b6-5efb-ac6c-fdd6070d629a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}28 & 63 \\\\ -82 & -100\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530879} {:answer/id #uuid "53a94891-9fff-54e9-9526-058c5c41499e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}28 & 63 \\\\ -82 & -102\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531048} {:answer/id #uuid "80dc457b-40f0-5416-88c9-738158bc9b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}30 & 63 \\\\ -82 & -102\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531143} {:answer/id #uuid "91f65eed-1275-5875-bff6-728f5637d753" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}28 & 63 \\\\ -80 & -102\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531179} {:answer/id #uuid "f9268e4f-998a-54d3-9a35-6e0114243c06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}28 & 64 \\\\ -82 & -102\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #