frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}=C.\n$$\n\n- The function $z$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $z(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{z}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{z}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{z}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{z}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ {y}_{2} & {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=A{x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(z(y(x))){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}{|}_{{z}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531620 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204101 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "12de0411-fa8a-5be0-9d80-3e174cf92707" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Composition of Three Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34758535-7d4d-5931-8a1f-911be1bf1e6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}20 & -88 \\\\ -9 & 40\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530975} {:answer/id #uuid "7