t ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(z(y(x)))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $z\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $C$ and outputs a vector $f(z)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}=C.\n$$\n\n- The function $z$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $z(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{z}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{z}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{z}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{z}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2} & {y}_{1} \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=A{x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(z(y(x))){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}{|}_{{z}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-6 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-19 & 25 \\\\ 9 & -11\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}19 & -88 \\\\ -9 & 40\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531583 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204098 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "581d60ae-7926-5d60-a348-3c7fe045db06" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Dimensions of a Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a55c71a1-6223-529a-85bc-a9bbd3f063bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a55c71a1-6223-529a-85bc-a9bbd3f063bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531222} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dab6e0f-02b6-5411-b63f-a1bfaa3fd0fd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531422} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7a97c7a-56e4-52f0-aba0-4973d856abaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7a97c7a-56e4-52f0-aba0-4973d856abaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531368} :answer-field/id #uuid "7812b0c8-a1a4-5e93-9f3d-10a8a8685414" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531470} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6338d656-1841-5138-95f4-4b6378e8960e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6338d656-1841-5138-95f4-4b6378e8960e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531081} :answer-field/id #uuid "96b42a37-2c60-551c-8e86-744ef7115fed" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531485} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f75deb86-5e5d-5e2d-9cd9-fffa78c81d47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f75deb86-5e5d-5e2d-9cd9-fffa78c81d47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531367} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c7d5f96-b21f-5a6d-9152-c11e8ec482aa" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531493} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cbfad5d-2e5e-5ad2-9a54-aab932b7eb19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cbfad5d-2e5e-5ad2-9a54-aab932b7eb19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531028} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2fdc84c-26a3-52ee-83fa-56334143f205" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531524} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b1a8b6b-61be-54ef-8f09-df8cdccda60e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b1a8b6b-61be-54ef-8f09-df8cdccda60e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531065} :answer-field/id #uuid "db184784-f6d4-5c28-8a15-c15b05c79c8f" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531534}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3cd8cc0b-abb0-561c-b8fb-73430e8105db" :question/math-academy-id "q-270266" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{3}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2}^{3}-5{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}].\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{5} \\\\ 3{y}_{2}^{3}-{y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAccording to the chain rule, the derivative \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))\n$$\n\nis the product of a$\\,\\,${{field-1}}$\\times ${{field-2}} \nmatrix with a \n{{field-3}} $\\times $ {{field-4}} \nmatrix, which results in a \n{{field-5}} $\\times $ {{field-6}} \nmatrix." :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, the product\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nof a $2\\times 2$ matrix with a $2\\times 3$ matrix is a $2\\times 3$ matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531660 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204099 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e07aa16a-05a4-5cf7-8eba-bfe287efdf88" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Composition of Vector-Valued Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5357d450-abcf-50c3-96bd-a1511a8aa0b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5357d450-abcf-50c3-96bd-a1511a8aa0b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531047} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ca9696c-ed27-5b5d-bd05-4135421712bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531393} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "321d5e82-c48e-5811-888e-74d3e2581bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "321d5e82-c48e-5811-888e-74d3e2581bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530973} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9519eb4-2f77-527e-8bce-eeaa7fb7a398" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531532} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "709cce09-0567-5921-b471-91435e0f6347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "709cce09-0567-5921-b471-91435e0f6347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531114} :answer-field/id #uuid "df962cc0-8c0f-5244-9b84-5776766a0170" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531535}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fdb98924-99f5-55a4-8e7e-a090dae96539" :question/math-academy-id "q-270269" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}(2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}(2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{2} & 2{y}_{1} \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2} & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}2(1) \\\\ 3(-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(2{x}_{1}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(2{x}_{1}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(3{x}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(3{x}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 & -24 \\\\ 24 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531645 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204099 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e07aa16a-05a4-5cf7-8eba-bfe287efdf88" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Composition of Vector-Valued Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21a18e2b-10b2-54ed-a6ac-5c17d190f8ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21a18e2b-10b2-54ed-a6ac-5c17d190f8ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530937} :answer-field/id #uuid "3703a9d4-39d0-52e0-b2bc-ee344c22c3a9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531431} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5292515c-0fe0-52f1-9eb1-46ebf48da0df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5292515c-0fe0-52f1-9eb1-46ebf48da0df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531045} :answer-field/id #uuid "488426ab-dda7-531e-996c-ff2ec4f75627" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531445} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44580490-2fa0-570f-bccb-1ec9835cc25e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44580490-2fa0-570f-bccb-1ec9835cc25e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531010} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3e8934b-c392-5107-ac80-32d083b1ab1b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dac59390-e4c1-5a03-ac45-73be8ac0d42f" :question/math-academy-id "q-270271" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}-3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1} & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}2(1) \\\\ 1-3(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(2{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(2{x}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{2}-3{x}_{1}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{2}-3{x}_{1})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531611 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204099 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e07aa16a-05a4-5cf7-8eba-bfe287efdf88" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Composition of Vector-Valued Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35d55130-d4fa-5917-b1e0-af08ead2241c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35d55130-d4fa-5917-b1e0-af08ead2241c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530979} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c22a089-927d-5420-ba5b-9d5a307d76f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531392} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bad7d77-5b3b-5af2-8a59-8f057e347751" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bad7d77-5b3b-5af2-8a59-8f057e347751" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530991} :answer-field/id #uuid "e28c09c1-aa3c-5844-9e63-e8909dfcd99f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531538} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67ca7192-6580-54d4-9919-f42b30af00f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67ca7192-6580-54d4-9919-f42b30af00f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531095} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa3ff81f-7b33-5955-80fb-a94bca6abd34" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "78eabbdb-ae14-5218-80c9-de54367d95a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-270274" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{2}{y}_{2}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{3}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{2}{y}_{2}^{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{2}{y}_{2}^{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 2{y}_{1} & 1 \\\\ 2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}^{3} & 3{y}_{1}^{2}{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}1\\cdot (-1) \\\\ -{1}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(-{x}_{1}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(-{x}_{1}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & {x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531566 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204101 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "12de0411-fa8a-5be0-9d80-3e174cf92707" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Composition of Three Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18a20064-991f-5f64-8730-30df670fc1ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530912} {:answer/id #uuid "6be24f52-d6d5-5cdd-935d-3a061620637f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531105} {:answer/id #uuid "83f3c631-6095-5bc6-9751-a09c65e0edda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531152} {:answer/id #uuid "87da04e6-f999-5cb3-9b1f-26be1f323217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531160} {:answer/id #uuid "8ca00293-83cc-5c71-9ca0-c51f74e8d83c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83f3c631-6095-5bc6-9751-a09c65e0edda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531152} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a50b086-39a9-589d-8647-5c9e75a1557c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c1ab071-19e5-52c5-b033-ca671fa83041" :question/math-academy-id "q-270277" :question/problem "For $x,y,z\\in {R}^{2},$ consider the following functions: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & y(x)=Ax\\,\\text{where}\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & z(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & f(z)=Cz\\,\\text{where}\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(z(y(x)))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(z(y(x)))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $z\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $C$ and outputs a vector $f(z)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}=C.\n$$\n\n- The function $z$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $z(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{z}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{z}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{z}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{z}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2{y}_{1} & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=A{x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(z(y(x))){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}{|}_{{z}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
